{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "00X0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0003": "$u : \\mathcal{C} \\to \\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0004": "$(\\mathcal{I}_V^u)^{opp}$", "MATH_0005": "$u$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{D} \\to\n\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0007": "$u_s$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{section-functoriality-PSh}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-directed-morphism}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:133fc19ea63935c6e129e79eb451d08da0a2ee12f63e8b1458762b05c602678d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5e9c4c5aa90a6f29f0654c4f1d66816d48848addeda407dc170b6e45409749b0", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> be sites. Let\n<MATH_0003> be continuous.\nAssume all the categories <MATH_0004> of\nSection <REF_0001>\nare filtered. Then <MATH_0005> defines a morphism of sites <MATH_0006>, in other words <MATH_0007> is exact.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f894839dd3b5fc90eec2da8e0774047659cc60937ed7938efe910e87e72eb264", "unit_id": "tag:00X5:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "00X0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$u_s$", "MATH_0002": "$u^s$", "MATH_0003": "$u_s$", "MATH_0004": "$u_s$", "MATH_0005": "$u_s$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{I}_Y^{opp}$", "MATH_0007": "$u_p$", "MATH_0008": "$\\textit{PSh}$", "MATH_0009": "$u_s = \\# \\circ u_p$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-lemma-exact-adjoint}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{categories-lemma-directed-commutes}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{section-limits-colimits-PSh}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-sheafification-exact}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:34617cbd8f12916eae756e64e9a5fcf9feda7a3979f2464af4d3625a70074f6f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0a2a36ccd1530e92a827071e9190fde070eacfdbae911055cc326d3fc9398661", "source_text": "Since <MATH_0001> is the left adjoint of <MATH_0002> we see that <MATH_0003> is right\nexact, see Categories, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nHence it suffices to show that <MATH_0004> is left exact. In other words\nwe have to show that <MATH_0005> commutes with finite limits.\nBecause the categories <MATH_0006> are filtered\nwe see that <MATH_0007> commutes with finite limits, see\nCategories, Lemma <REF_0002>\n(this also uses the description of limits in <MATH_0008>,\nsee Section <REF_0003>).\nAnd since sheafification commutes with finite limits as well\n(Lemma <REF_0004>) we conclude because\n<MATH_0009>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:878e401c53b79975e95a102fed6f7b650d2c5942da5aa8933d58c3f1566e1d0a", "unit_id": "tag:00X5:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "proposition", "parent_tag": "00X0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0003": "$u : \\mathcal{C} \\to \\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "MATH_0006": "$u(X)$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0009": "$u$", "MATH_0010": "$u$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{D} \\to\n\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0012": "$u_s$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proposition}\n\\label{proposition-get-morphism}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proposition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:621f3de2e8323d3d457bcc0a3aa779437ecd2272977916b0fca978cf512acb7b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7531eec99f7a26b73f6f650aa53e5329958574b40d8e963e555d053f5de19d74", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> be sites. Let\n<MATH_0003> be continuous.\nAssume furthermore the following:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> the category <MATH_0004> has a final object <MATH_0005> and\n<MATH_0006> is a final object of <MATH_0007> , and\n<STRUCT_0003> the category <MATH_0008> has fibre products and\n<MATH_0009> commutes with them.\n<STRUCT_0004>\nThen <MATH_0010> defines a morphism of sites <MATH_0011>, in other words <MATH_0012> is exact.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:411a400487b491662d3cd5ecfc6d4313a72da8fa9547b8818bb12d242886e41e", "unit_id": "tag:00X6:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "00X0", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-directed}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-directed-morphism}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:92a2a70ca6d161c8dee43e3bb6e592fc11c14aba4375e2468a5c6374b8a24b80", "source_text": "This follows from Lemmas <REF_0001> and\n<REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1fbc42529683590f32949e3faa1d95f9e5812186ef9dae7a4dbbabe1143702f8", "unit_id": "tag:00X6:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "00X0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$u$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{proposition-get-morphism}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{categories-lemma-finite-limits-exist}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{categories-lemma-characterize-left-exact}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-explain-left-exact}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:cfde279af4afcaf08e521d7d0c116b7c6233b70a2d805d0bd17d76ece89e7b9c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1bdba3478281d4fc88ad9d31b72aa2cca5cb5115005b983dba95ba49b4c407d9", "source_text": "The conditions of Proposition <REF_0001> above\nare equivalent to saying that <MATH_0001> is left exact, i.e., commutes\nwith finite limits. See\nCategories, Lemmas\n<REF_0002> and\n<REF_0003>.\nIt seems more natural to phrase it in terms of final objects\nand fibre products since this seems to have more geometric meaning\nin the examples.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3862a9b1e972ed181ea5a75efa7228259c22c4c7333ba212e1d239d38e88ab20", "unit_id": "tag:00X7:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "00X0", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-continuous-with-continuous-left-adjoint}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d4a55e8c7e7f0c2d089c243847363f94c1626b11dc256e176b27614b3a57ee52", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLemma <REF_0001> will\nprovide another way to prove a continuous functor\ngives rise to a morphism of sites.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:647fb3e93b983cc71a9a558f49c57ca5f3d332edb07e5f8f6913fbe273d2608f", "unit_id": "tag:00X0:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "00X0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0003": "$f : \\mathcal{D} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$u : \\mathcal{C} \\to \\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0005": "$u_s$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-morphism-sites}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{remark-quasi-continuous}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{proposition-get-morphism}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-quasi-continuous-morphism-sites}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:750c0231b84af082cca566c81778e9b14469921158fcfec20532b841502861bf", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cda5092ec0a3e8a23bf96d59997d196569c823f6496cb0f2ab6361a534a22a98", "source_text": "(Skip on first reading.)\nLet <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> be sites. Analogously to\nDefinition <REF_0001> we say that\na <TEXTITOPEN_0001>quasi-morphism of sites <MATH_0003><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nis given by a quasi-continuous functor <MATH_0004>\n(see Remark <REF_0002>) such that <MATH_0005> is exact.\nThe analogue of Proposition <REF_0003> in this\nsetting is obtained by replacing the word ``continuous''\nby the word ``quasi-continuous'', and replacing the word\n``morphism'' by ``quasi-morphism''. The proof is literally the\nsame.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1c57faecf19418f09c91b283225ac48356b2fb859233828575821367bd5ce276", "unit_id": "tag:00X8:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "00X0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$u_s$", "MATH_0002": "$u$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-morphism-sites}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6a3e431b36c46a8db4e459219122316d86fd95e9f757ff09f36cbb888599e7c3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:37685dc08414d88080adea050ec368b396a9d75de3504f2a0da7b007a5cc501b", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn Definition <REF_0001> the condition that <MATH_0001>\nbe exact cannot be omitted. For example, the conclusion of the following\nlemma need not hold if one only assumes that <MATH_0002> is continuous.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b8c67d35c921c2b76a6094f0c63457f7de3e9095c73f3382e5c0dbd002051891", "unit_id": "tag:00X0:prose-0004"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "00X0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{D} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$u : \\mathcal{C} \\to \\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0003": "$V$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{V_j \\to V\\}$", "MATH_0006": "$j$", "MATH_0007": "$V_j \\to u(U_j)$", "MATH_0008": "$U_j$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{C}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-morphism-of-sites-covering}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1755ca08d49b7fff2c6506424c412ebb11315e72be0f23ba93673e500fbd58b4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:74ca7928d131c44e40d33a221c582977c5a85cfd2623eead34c5607ebfe0037e", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of sites given by the\nfunctor <MATH_0002>. Given any object <MATH_0003> of\n<MATH_0004> there exists a covering <MATH_0005> such that for every\n<MATH_0006> there exists a morphism <MATH_0007> for some object <MATH_0008>\nof <MATH_0009>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:04d7f14028ecdfed0ead14ff7b08bfc7481de7ec438021e9559fa8fb5c15b536", "unit_id": "tag:08H2:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "00X0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f^{-1} = u_s$", "MATH_0002": "$f^{-1}* = *$", "MATH_0003": "$*$", "MATH_0004": "$f^{-1}* = u_s*$", "MATH_0005": "$u_p*$", "MATH_0006": "$\\{V_j \\to V\\}$", "MATH_0007": "$(u_p*)(V_j)$", "MATH_0008": "$(u_p*)(V_j)$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{I}^u_{V_j}$", "MATH_0010": "$V_j \\to u(U)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{example-singleton-sheaf}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6467fa790b27437a8e02387843647060384b3a137c838d03d4ca7513818dcb14", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6245236edf0af3506104d2f27fddc1c9b5806acce38c5b1b37fce9d6b291ae9d", "source_text": "Since <MATH_0001> is exact we have <MATH_0002> where <MATH_0003> denotes the\nfinal object of the category of sheaves\n(Example <REF_0001>).\nSince <MATH_0004> is the sheafification of <MATH_0005> we see\nthere exists a covering <MATH_0006> such that <MATH_0007>\nis nonempty. Since <MATH_0008> is a colimit over the category\n<MATH_0009> whose objects are morphisms <MATH_0010>\nthe lemma follows.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:38b2251336ae7555cb11f450b6b3e85e93c9dbbdfea66b61317475cdcb24213d", "unit_id": "tag:08H2:proof"}
